A's labor.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 locates the kitchen and oven, and A3 gives a concrete four-hour investment.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'shelf has a history' is vague, while A5's oven partnership risks a separate personification joke.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you put the pizza in, admire the oven. Four hours.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's spotless. Can I cook? I'm starving.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Notice the rack as you slide it in. That was an hour.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll buy you dinner if we can keep it clean tonight.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. We can toast the other three hours.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes otherwise unnoticed labor visible and engineers increasingly specific opportunities for appreciation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wanting praise for a possession.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 cites four hours of cleaning; revised A3 assigns one hour to the rack, locating the desired appreciation in A's work.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a turns a hungry partner's dinner offer into quantified recognition; b uses displayed household objects and a proposed redistribution of chores.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the weak relationship and drifting final image. The kitchen setting remains, with pizza preparation added. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 expose hours worked); logic 5 (B2's cooking uses the rack in A3; B4's dinner offer becomes A5's toast); relationship 4 (B2 wants food and B4 bargains); heightening 4 (A5 extends recognition to all remaining hours); specificity 5 (A1 establishes imminent cooking); brevity/wit 4 (A5's arithmetic earns the toast). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No human or live review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The final toast is a modest escalation; performance should preserve sincere appreciation-seeking rather than sarcastic punishment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S42-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7e3961c998e06e10887e4f2fc154d7cc25c31e8ceaccbe13a28c2679ae96a735\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 displays evidence of laundry; A3 calls it a memorial; A5 creates another opportunity to appreciate folded towels.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2's question elicits A3's explanation, but A5's towel invitation could follow almost any acknowledgment at B4.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 asks why and B4 thanks A, without pursuing dinner or responding to the intrusive display.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds towels to the memorial conceit, but B4 provides little new pressure or choice.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's empty detergent bottle beside dinner makes the household reminder concrete and playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's memorial and A5's visitors share a concise exhibition conceit.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've put the empty detergent bottle beside your dinner.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can it move? I need room for my plate.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. It represents six loads, if you're wondering.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Six? I'll do the laundry tomorrow.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Thank you. Come and see how I fold the towels, so you know what you're taking on.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A makes otherwise unnoticed labor visible and engineers increasingly specific opportunities for appreciation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply asking for help with chores.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 displays a spent bottle and A3 supplies the load count before B offers help; A5 converts that offer into a tour of existing work.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses a conspicuous display and B's offer to share labor; a extracts detailed recognition through a dinner invitation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised B's passive contributions while preserving the detergent-at-dinner setting. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 display otherwise invisible work); logic 5 (B2's space request prompts A3's removal with a reminder; B4's takeover prompts A5's demonstration); relationship 4 (B2 wants dining space and B4 offers relief); heightening 4 (A5 extends recognition into a practical tour); specificity 5 (A1 supplies the dinner obstruction); brevity/wit 4 (A3's six loads gives the bottle its pointed purpose). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No human or live review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 can sound like ordinary instruction unless the actor gives weight to showing how much work the towels represent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S43-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"7b0e5c354fc8f372744fe8cf2e3e4d574492d8c3b3ccc91545d347b80ece33f0\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 protects tea-shoes-keys and A3 restarts tea, but A5 leaves the feared wider chaos unspecified.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 follows the early key touch in A1 more directly than B2's lateness; A5 answers B4 with a generic warning.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to leave on time and B4 proposes holding keys while the kettle boils.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the need for order without increasing the consequence of B4's proposed overlap.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives actors tea, shoes and keys in a recognizable departure routine.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's restart is concise, but A5's 'find out why' withholds the specific comic consequence.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tea, then shoes, then keys. You've picked up the keys before we've had tea.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're late for the train.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we especially need the usual order. Otherwise we'll forget the tickets too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll hold the tickets while you drink.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tickets go in after shoes. Please don't make us start packing again.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A protects an established sequence because changing one step appears to threaten the reliability of everything that follows.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Arbitrary bossiness.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 predicts forgotten tickets from a broken sequence, and A5 treats B's helpful overlap as grounds to restart packing.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a expands a threatened departure ritual under time pressure; b treats the routine as necessary to establish the cat's morning despite the actual clock.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the weak B2-to-A3 link and generic ending. The departure setting and tea-shoes-keys sequence remain; train tickets make the feared cascade concrete. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 connect disruption to further disorder); logic 5 (B2's train makes tickets relevant in A3; B4's ticket offer triggers A5's packing reset); relationship 4 (B4 tries to help them leave); heightening 4 (A5 threatens a larger restart); specificity 5 (A1/B2 establish the departure); brevity/wit 4 (A5 earns its escalation through the offered tickets). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No human or live review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The ticket step is revealed late, though it extends the existing departure routine coherently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S43-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"91f4fe11c6f117502f38099c91399dda015cda98163c2b61ef6ed269eaeb3c58\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 makes curtains necessary to establish morning; A5 interprets midday as evidence of disorder already affecting the cat.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's hunger prompts A3's prerequisite; B4's midday correction becomes A5's reason to protect that prerequisite.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the hungry cat fed and B4 challenges the ritual with the actual time.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs contradictory evidence as proof that the routine is now even more necessary.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes curtains before cat food in a familiar household routine.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Exactly' economically converts B4's correction into support for A's position.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We always open the curtains before feeding the cat.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The cat's hungry now.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The curtains establish morning.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's midday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. We've already confused the cat enough.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A protects an established sequence because changing one step appears to threaten the reliability of everything that follows.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Superstitious belief about curtains.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names a familiar ordered routine, and A5 reads the disrupted day as harm caused by departing from that order.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b defends domestic temporal order through the cat's supposed confusion; a escalates a departure routine through threatened packing resets.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: the correction in B4 specifically strengthens A's existing belief in A5. Acceptance and hard gates pass without rewriting.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The threatened chaos remains small and partly implicit: a confused cat stands in for wider household disorder.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S44-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"58c76e5cdf964175941600ef70ee6994d17b2cdb78406b3222c6afd33a90d08f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 packs two torches and A5 adds chargers to support B4's proposed phone backups.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's noon objection; A5 specifically reclassifies B4's phones as backup torches.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions unnecessary picnic equipment and B4 offers equipment they already carry.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 absorbs B4's simplifying solution into another layer of emergency supplies.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's picnic and two torches immediately establish practical packing choices.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'backup torches' earns its joke by using B4's phones; A3's late noon is more stylized.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 88\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've packed two torches for the picnic.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're going at noon.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"In case noon runs late.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We can use our phones.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. I've packed chargers for your backup torches.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A meets ordinary uncertainty and proposed solutions by adding backups against their possible failure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General pessimism.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 supplies chargers for B4's phones, turning worry into practical redundancy rather than merely predicting trouble.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a welcomes B's solution and equips it; b interrogates a roadside fallback until it reveals A's existing duplicate phones.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: B4's helpful proposal becomes the next expression of the card in A5. Acceptance and hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's 'noon runs late' requires the ordinary inference that the picnic may extend beyond its planned time.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S44-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"dfd6abff4782c1bf12ffc84d8ceb8bba4e5564b33ebe83f9c63342973239d065\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requests a spare jack; A3 anticipates the existing jack breaking; A5 reveals two packed phones.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's jack becomes A3's failure scenario, and B4's call for help becomes A5's phone redundancy.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 defends the existing equipment and B4 proposes outside help rather than more tools.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends preparation beyond mechanical equipment to the means of summoning rescue.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes vehicle preparation through a spare tyre and jack, though the trip itself is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's short failure question sets up A5's compact reveal of duplicate phones.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The spare tyre's ready. Where's the spare jack?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's already a jack.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And when that breaks?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We'll call for help.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"On which of the two phones I've packed?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A meets ordinary uncertainty and proposed solutions by adding backups against their possible failure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Competent one-time preparation.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 wants a spare for the tool used with a spare, and A5 reveals another duplicated fallback after B4 proposes rescue.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b exposes nested preparation through questioning; a cooperatively adds support to B's suggested phones.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading: both B turns supply the precise fallback A next scrutinizes. Acceptance and hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 reveals prior preparation rather than making a fresh commitment, so the heightening is principally a widening of scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S45-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"efc61c4e05c1daa794b85820ca827ca6f5192369c18423de82d975db3d0e7c2f\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 calls spilled shopping an outdoor class and A5 converts wet bread into soup night.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's pavement prompts A3's outdoor lesson; B4's wet bread supplies A5's soup idea.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 identify practical problems, but B has no developed preference or initiative.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 proposes a different meal, though it does not develop A3's shared cooking-class opportunity.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's split shopping bag and B2's pavement make the mishap clear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's rolling-tomato lesson is vivid, but A5's wet-bread soup risks sounding like an isolated salvage joke.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 72\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The shopping bag split. Lovely, now we can sort dinner before we get home.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The tomatoes are crushed. I wanted sandwiches.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We've accidentally started pasta sauce. You always say we should cook together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Only if you let me handle the seasoning this time.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Deal. The bag's improved dinner and got me to share the kitchen.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets each mishap as a welcome opportunity to improve the plan or the relationship.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Cheerful denial of damage.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 changes the damaged ingredients into a shared cooking plan, and A5 accepts a real change in kitchen control.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a turns food damage into cooking together and sharing authority; b uses a cancelled repair and continuing inconvenience to reclaim time together.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to give the opportunity relational consequences. The split-shopping-bag setting remains; the ingredients and dinner preference are clarified. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 welcome the mishap as improvement); logic 5 (B2's tomatoes cause sauce in A3; B4's condition causes A5's concession); relationship 5 (B4 claims meaningful kitchen authority); heightening 4 (A5 credits the mishap with changing their habits); specificity 5 (A1/B2 establish damaged shopping and dinner); brevity/wit 4 (A5's praise of the bag follows the bargain). Total 95. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No human or live review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 states the benefit fairly explicitly; its warmth is stronger than its surprise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S45-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3cfb4d96bf898852c8c0323107dc27d5f56f0038ad747cc952437c9e2947080c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 welcomes the cancellation, but A5's benefit is merely not hearing the unresolved leak.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's leak prompts relocation in A3; B4's rain becomes sound cover in A5.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 keeps attention on the repair and B4 challenges the garden plan, but A offers little shared gain.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 rebrands another inconvenience without making the afternoon a more productive or bonding opportunity.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a cancelled plumber and A3 supplies a concrete garden lunch.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's rain masking the sink is concise and causally linked, though closer to avoidance than discovery.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The plumber's cancelled. Lovely, we can finally have lunch together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The sink still leaks. I've put a bucket under it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Excellent. The bucket's covering the sink; I'll set the table.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It needs emptying every ten minutes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we'll have courses. Neither of us can rush off with a sandwich.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets each mishap as a welcome opportunity to improve the plan or the relationship.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Avoiding an unpleasant problem.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 incorporates B's containment measure, and A5 makes its recurring maintenance a reason for a longer shared lunch.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b turns delay and ongoing maintenance into protected companionship; a turns damaged ingredients into shared cooking and a concession over control.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the avoidance ending into a concrete bonding opportunity. The cancelled-plumber setting remains; a bucket replaces the garden excursion. Separate internal reread, coach-1.0: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 welcome disruption as time together); logic 5 (B2's bucket enables A3's lunch; B4's interval determines A5's courses); relationship 4 (B manages the leak while A seeks company); heightening 4 (A5 makes continued inconvenience prolong the occasion); specificity 5 (B2/B4 establish the practical maintenance); brevity/wit 4 (A5's courses convert the ten-minute constraint economically). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No human or live review.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The bucket is temporary containment; 